              "@id": "urn:uuid:6f6aad8e-ae81-5770-b9a8-8615919bfe8e",
              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Case 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 1 of 14 PageID.381\nOR\\G\\NAL\nFILED IN THE\nUNITED STi\\TES DISTRICT COURT\nCLARE E . CONNORS #7936 DISTRICT OF /-INNi\\11\nUnited States Attorney\nDistrict of Hawaii lr JUL 2 5 2024\nat_ o'clock and o\n1 min.f M C(,A_.,,\nREBECCA A. PERLMUTTER Lucy H. Carrillo, Clerk\nAssistant United States Attorney\nRoom 6-100, PJKK Federal Building\n300 Ala Moana Boulevard\nHonolulu, Hawaii 96850\nTelephone: (808) 541-2850\nFax: (808) 541-2958\nEmail: Rebecca.Perlmutter@usdoj .gov\n\nAttorneys for Plaintiff\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA\n\nIN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n\nFOR THE DISTRICT OF HAWAH\n\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA, ) CR. N O. 23-0007 1 JMS\n)\nPlaintiff, ) SUPERSEDING INDICTMENT\n)\nvs. ) [1 8 U .S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 1591(a)(l), 1591(b)(2),\n) 2251(a), 2251(e), 2252(a)(2),\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, ) 2252(a)(4)(B), 2252(b)(2), and\n) 2422(b)]\nDefendant. )\n\nSUPERSEDING INDICTMENT\n\nThe Grand Jury charges:\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 2 of 14 PageID.382\n\nCOUNTl\nProduction of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2251(a) and 2251(e))\n\nIn or around summer 2019, within the District of Hawaii and elsewhere,\n\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did employ, use, persuade, induce,\n\nentice, and coerce \"Minor Victim 1\" (\"MV 1\"), a minor, to engage in sexually\n\nexplicit conduct for the purpose of producing any visual depiction of such conduct,\n\nnamely an approximately 51-second video involving MVl engaged in sexually\n\nexplicit conduct, knowing and having reason to know that any such visual\n\ndepiction would be transported and transmitted using any means and facility of\n\ninterstate and foreign commerce and in and affecting such commerce, and where\n\nany such visual depiction was produced using materials that had been mailed,\n\nshipped, and transported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any\n\nmeans, including by computer, and where any such visual depiction was actually\n\ntransported and transmitted using any means and facility of interstate and foreign\n\ncommerce and in and affecting such commerce, and did attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 2251 (a) and 2251 ( e).\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n2\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 3 of 14 PageID.383\n\nCOUNT2\nProduction of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 225l{a) and 225l(e))\n\nIn or around summer 2019, within the District of Hawaii and elsewhere,\n\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did employ, use, persuade, induce,\n\nentice, and coerce MVl, a minor, to engage in sexually explicit conduct for the\n\npurpose of producing any visual depiction of such conduct, namely an\n\napproximately 16-second video involving MV 1 engaged in sexually explicit\n\nconduct, knowing and having reason to know that any such visual depiction would\n\nbe transported and transmitted using any means and facility of interstate and\n\nforeign commerce and in and affecting such commerce, and where any such visual\n\ndepiction was produced using materials that had been mailed, shipped, and\n\ntransported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any means,\n\nincluding by computer, and where any such visual depiction was actually\n\ntransported and transmitted using any means and facility of interstate and foreign\n\ncommerce and in and affecting such commerce, and did attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation ofTitle 18, United States Code, Sections 2251(a) and 2251(e).\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n3\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 4 of 14 PageID.384\n\nCOUNT3\nProduction of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2251(a) and 2251(e))\n\nIn or around August 2019, within the District of Hawaii and elsewhere,\n\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did employ, use, persuade, induce,\n\nentice, and coerce \"Minor Victim 2\" (\"MV2\"), a minor, to engage in sexually\n\nexplicit conduct for the purpose of producing any visual depiction of such conduct,\n\nnamely an approximately 22-second video involving MV2 engaged in sexually\n\nexplicit conduct, knowing and having reason to know that any such visual\n\ndepiction would be transported and transmitted using any means and facility of\n\ninterstate and foreign commerce and in and affecting such commerce, and where\n\nany such visual depiction was produced using materials that had been mailed,\n\nshipped, and transported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any\n\nmeans, including by computer, and where any such visual depiction was actually\n\ntransported and transmitted using any means and facility of interstate and foreign\n\ncommerce and in and affecting such commerce, and did attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 2251 (a) and 2251 (e).\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n4\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 5 of 14 PageID.385\n\nCOUNT4\nSex Trafficking a Minor\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 1591(a){l) and 159l{b)(2))\n\nFrom in our around August 2019, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, the defendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did knowingly recruit,\n\nentice, harbor, transport, obtain, maintain, and solicit by any means, in and\n\naffecting interstate and foreign commerce, MV2, having reasonable opportunity to\n\nobserve MV2 and knowing and in reckless disregard of the fact that MV2 had not\n\nattained the age of 18 years and that MV2 would be caused to engage in a\n\ncommercial sex act, and did attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 1591(a)(l) and\n\n1591 (b )(2).\n\nCOUNTS\nDistribution of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252(a)(2) and 2252(b)(l))\n\nIn or around August 2019, within the District of Hawaii and elsewhere,\n\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did knowingly distribute any visual\n\ndepiction to MV2, using any means and facility of interstate and foreign\n\ncommerce, and which visual depiction had been mailed, shipped, and transported\n\nin and affecting interstate and foreign commerce, and which contained materials\n\nwhich had been mailed and so shipped and transported by any means, including by\n\ncomputer, and the production of such visual depiction involved the use of a minor\n\n5\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 6 of 14 PageID.386\n\nengaging in sexually explicit conduct, and such visual depiction was of such\n\nconduct, and did attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Section 2252(a)(2) and\n\n2252(b)( 1).\n\nCOUNT6\nSex Trafficking a Minor\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 159l(a)(l) and 1591(b)(2))\n\nFrom in or around January to August 2020, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, the defendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did knowingly recruit,\n\nentice, harbor, transport, obtain, maintain, and solicit by any means, in and\n\naffecting interstate and foreign commerce, \"Minor Victim 3\" (\"MV3 \"), having\n\nreasonable opportunity to observe MV3 and knowing and in reckless disregard of\n\nthe fact that MV3 had not attained the age of 18 years and that MV3 would be\n\ncaused to engage in a commercial sex act, and did attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 1591(a)(l) and\n\n1591 (b)(2).\n\nCOUNT7\nCoercion and Enticement of a Minor\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b))\n\nFrom in or around January to August 2020, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, the defendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did use any facility and\n\nmeans of interstate and foreign commerce, namely the Internet and a cellular\n\n6\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 7 of 14 PageID.387\n\nphone, to knowingly persuade, induce, entice, and coerce MV3, an individual who\n\nhad not attained the age of 18 years, to engage in sexual activity under such\n\ncircumstances as would constitute a criminal offense under Hawaii state law,\n\nnamely Hawaii Revised Statutes, Sections 707-730(1)(c) and 707-732(1)(c), and\n\ndid attempt to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Section 2422(b).\n\nCOUNTS\nReceipt of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2252(a)(2))\n\nOn or about May 16, 2020, within the District of Hawaii and elsewhere, the\n\ndefendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did knowingly receive any visual\n\ndepiction, using any means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce, and\n\nwhich visual depiction had been mailed, shipped, and transported in and affecting\n\ninterstate and foreign commerce, and which contained materials which had been\n\nmailed and so shipped and transported by any means, including by computer, and\n\nthe production of such visual depiction involved the use ofMV3, a minor,\n\nengaging in sexually explicit conduct, and such visual depiction was of such\n\nconduct.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Section 2252(a)(2).\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n7\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 8 of 14 PageID.388\n\nCOUNT9\nSex Trafficking a Minor\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 159l{a)(l) and 1591(b)(2))\n\nFrom in or around July 2019 to September 2020, within the District of\n\nHawaii and elsewhere, the defendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did knowingly\n\nrecruit, entice, harbor, transport, obtain, maintain, and solicit by any means, in and\n\naffecting interstate and foreign commerce, \"Minor Victim 4\" (\"MV4\"), having\n\nreasonable opportunity to observe MV4 and knowing and in reckless disregard of\n\nthe fact that MV4 had not attained the age of 18 years and that MV4 would be\n\ncaused to engage in a commercial sex act, and attempted to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 1591(a)(l) and\n\n1591(b)(2).\n\nCOUNTl0\nCoercion and Enticement of a Minor\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b))\n\nFrom in or around July to August 2019, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, the defendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did use any facility and\n\nmeans of interstate and foreign commerce, namely the Internet and a cellular\n\nphone, to knowingly persuade, induce, entice, and coerce MV4, an individual who\n\nhad not attained the age of 18 years, to engage in sexual activity under such\n\ncircumstances as would constitute a criminal offense under Hawaii state law,\n\n8\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 9 of 14 PageID.389\n\nnamely Hawaii Revised Statutes, Sections 707-730(1)(c) and 707-732(1)(c), and\n\nattempted to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Section 2422(b).\n\nCOUNT 11\nSex Trafficking a Minor\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 159l(a)(l) and 159l(b)(2))\n\nFrom in or around July to August 2020, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, the defendant, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, did knowingly recruit,\n\nentice, harbor, transport, obtain, maintain, and solicit by any means, in and\n\naffecting interstate and foreign commerce, \"Minor Victim 5\" (\"MV5\"), having\n\nreasonable opportunity to observe MV 5 and knowing and in reckless disregard of\n\nthe fact that MV 5 had not attained the age of 18 years and that MV5 would be\n\ncaused to engage in a commercial sex act, and attempted to do so.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 1591(a)(l) and\n\n1591 (b)(2).\n\nCOUNT12\nPossession of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252(a)(4)(B) and 2252(b )(2))\n\nOn or about December 14, 2022, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did knowingly possess\n\nany matter which contained any visual depiction that had been mailed, shipped,\n\nand transported using any means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce\n\n9\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 10 of 14 PageID.390\n\nand in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce, and which was produced\n\nusing materials which had been mailed and so shipped and transported by any\n\nmeans, including by computer, and the production of such visual depiction\n\ninvolved the use of a minor engaged in sexually explicit conduct, including a\n\nprepubescent minor and a minor who had not attained 12 years of age, and such\n\nvisual depiction was of such conduct.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 2252(a)(4)(B) and\n\n2252(b)(2).\n\nFIRST FORFEITURE NOTICE\n\n1. The allegations in Counts 1 through 3, 5, 8, and 12 of this\n\nSuperseding Indictment are incorporated here for the purpose of noticing\n\nforfeitures pursuant to Title 18, United States Code, Section 2253.\n\n2. The United States hereby gives notice to DARREN PATRICK\n\nRILEY, the defendant, that, upon conviction of an offense in violation of Title 18,\n\nUnited States Code, Sections 2251 and 2252, the United States will seek forfeiture,\n\nin accordance with Title 18, United States Code, Section 2253, of (a) any visual\n\ndepiction described in Title 18, United States Code, Section 2252, and any book,\n\nmagazine, periodical, film, videotape, or other matter which contains any such\n\nvisual depiction, which was produced, transported, mailed, shipped, or received in\n\nviolation of that section; (b) any property, real or personal, constituting or traceable\n\n10\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 11 of 14 PageID.391\n\nto gross profits or other proceeds obtained from such offense; and (c) any property,\n\nreal or personal, used or intended to be used to commit or to promote the\n\ncommission of such offense or any property traceable to such property.\n\n3. If by any act or omission of the defendant, any of the property subject\n\nto forfeiture described in the preceding paragraph herein:\n\na. cannot be located upon the exercise of due diligence;\n\nb. has been transferred or sold to, or deposited with, a third party;\n\nc. has been placed beyond the jurisdiction of the court;\n\nd. has been substantially diminished in value; or\n\ne. has been commingled with other property which cannot be subdivided\n\nwithout difficulty,\n\nthe United States will be entitled to forfeiture of substitute property up to the value\n\nof the property described above in the preceding paragraph, pursuant to Title 21,\n\nUnited States Code, Section 853(p), as incorporated by Title 18, United States\n\nCode, Section 2253.\n\nSECOND FORFEITURE NOTICE\n\nI. The allegations in Counts 4, 6, and 10 of this Superseding Indictment\n\nare incorporated here for the purpose of noticing forfeitures pursuant to Title 18,\n\nUnited States Code, Section 1594.\n\n11\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 12 of 14 PageID.392\n\n2. The United States hereby gives notice to DARREN PATRICK\n\nRILEY, the defendant, that, upon conviction of an offense in violation of Title 18,\n\nUnited States Code, Section 1591(a)(l), the United States will seek forfeiture, in\n\naccordance with Title 18, United States Code, Section 1594, of (a)\n\ndefendant's interest in any property, real or personal, that was involved in, used,\n\nor intended to be used to commit or to facilitate the commission of such violation,\n\nand any property traceable to such property; and (b) any property, real or personal,\n\nconstituting or derived from, any proceeds that such person obtained, directly or\n\nindirectly, as a result of such violation, or any property traceable to such property.\n\n3. If by any act or omission of the defendant, any of the property subject\n\nto forfeiture described in the preceding paragraph herein:\n\na. cannot be located upon the exercise of due diligence;\n\nb. has been transferred or sold to, or deposited with, a third party;\n\nc. has been placed beyond the jurisdiction of the court;\n\nd. has been substantially diminished in value; or\n\ne. has been commingled with other property which cannot be subdivided\n\nwithout difficulty,\n\nthe United States will be entitled to forfeiture of substitute property up to the value\n\nof the property described above in the preceding paragraph, pursuant to Title 21,\n\nUnited States Code, Section 853(p), as incorporated by Title 18, United States\n\n12\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 13 of 14 PageID.393\n\nCode, Section 2253.\n\nTHIRD FORFEITURE NOTICE\n\n1. The allegations in Counts 7 and 11 of this Superseding Indictment are\n\nincorporated here for the purpose of noticing forfeitures pursuant to Title 18,\n\nUnited States Code, Sections 2428.\n\n2. The United States hereby gives notice to DARREN PATRICK\n\nRILEY, the defendant, that, upon conviction of an offense in violation of Title 18,\n\nUnited States Code, Section 2422(b ), the United States will seek forfeiture, in\n\naccordance with Title 18, United States Code, Section 2428, of (a) defendant's\n\ninterest in any property, real or personal, that was used or intended to be used to\n\ncommit or to facilitate the commission of such violation; and (b) any property, real\n\nor personal, constituting or derived from any proceeds that such person obtained,\n\ndirectly or indirectly, as a result of such violation.\n\n3. If by any act or omission of the defendant, any of the property subject\n\nto forfeiture described in the preceding paragraph herein:\n\na. cannot be located upon the exercise of due diligence;\n\nb. has been transferred or sold to, or deposited with, a third party;\n\nc. has been placed beyond the jurisdiction of the court;\n\nd. has been substantially diminished in value; or\n\ne. has been commingled with other property which cannot be subdivided\n\n13\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 70 Filed 07/25/24 Page 14 of 14 PageID.394\n\nwithout difficulty,\n\nthe United States will be entitled to forfeitw-e of substitute property up to the value\n\nof the property described above in the preceding paragraph, pursuant to Title 21 ,\n\nUnited States Code, Section 853(p), as incorporated by Title 18, United States\n\nCode, Section 2253.\n\nDATED: July 2.5 , 2024, at Honolulu, Hawaii.\n\nIsl Foreperson\n\nGRAND JURY FOREPERSON\n\n~I 07,-d\nCLARE E. CONNORS\nUnited States Attorney\nDistrict of Hawaii\n\n~~~\nREBECCA A . PERLMUTTER\nAssistant U.S. Attorney\n\nUnited States v. Darren Patrick Riley\nCr. No. 23-00071 JMS\nSuperseding Indictment\n\n14"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
